Steps to create .bif and .sim formatted vectors from the BusTalk
code (default)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
make <testname>

This will create infile.bif and bif.sim in the ./invec directory

Please refer to the 'makefile' for legal 'testname's.

RUNNING THE COMPLETE TEST SUITE
===============================
All the tests for the Smc cannot be run together because of the 
large bif/tif files that will be created because of the large number of test
cases presnt. Instead the tests have been partitioned into 6 sub-tests to 
facilitate running the complete tests.
They are :
1. Smc1
2. Smc2
3. Smc3
4. Smc4
5. Smc5
6. Smc6

Please note that Smc1-6 can be run for rtl simulations, but for netlist 
simulations only Smc1-5 should be run.

Please compile these tests seperately, and issue make rtl from the top level 
each time to run the tests. For example, the following set of commands will
compile and run all the tests. After setting all the environment variables 
metioned in the smc_pl092/README file.

From the smc_pl092 directory:

cd verification/bustest
make Smc1
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make rtl

cd ../bustest
make Smc2
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make rtl

cd ../bustest
make Smc3
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make rtl

cd ../bustest
make Smc4
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make -f denali.mk rtl

cd ../bustest
make Smc5
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make -f denali.mk TBENCH=1 rtl

cd ../bustest
make Smc6
cd ../${HDL_SOURCE}
make rtl

Alternatively, the above set of commands can be copied into a file, and run
from the top level to perform the tests, with suitable commands to rename the
logs which are generated so that they are not overwritten by subsequent tests.

